    "rating": "HIGH",
    "description": "Rated on its DRAM leadership, its peak position, not on HBM where it is a substitutable non-leader (peak-position ruling). Samsung is the number-one maker in the three-supplier DRAM oligopoly (Samsung, SK Hynix, Micron); a memory buyer cannot leave that oligopoly, and requalifying volume away from the category leader is a multi-quarter, multi-billion undertaking. On HBM specifically Samsung lags SK Hynix and would rate lower, but the grade attaches to the strongest frontier position, which for Samsung is DRAM. Category-dominant with a costly-but-possible substitute, which is what HIGH means.",
